DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddccoonnsscchhaatt utility is designed to provide a way for users to access
     dcons(4) (dumb console device) on a local or remote system.  The
     ddccoonnsscchhaatt utility interacts with dcons(4) using kvm(3) or firewire(4),
     and interacts with the user over TTY or TCP/IP.  To access remote
     dcons(4) using firewire(4), you have to specify target EUI64 address us‐
     ing the --tt option. Physical DMA should be enabled on the target machine
     for access via FireWire.

     The ddccoonnsscchhaatt utility and the dcons(4) driver communicate using 2 ports,
     one for the console port and another for remote gdb(1) (_p_o_r_t_s_/_d_e_v_e_l_/_g_d_b)
     port.  Users are supposed to access ddccoonnsscchhaatt using TTY, telnet(1) and
     gdb(1) (_p_o_r_t_s_/_d_e_v_e_l_/_g_d_b).  You can specify listen ports for console and
     gdb(1) (_p_o_r_t_s_/_d_e_v_e_l_/_g_d_b) port using the --CC and --GG options respectively.
     The port number 0 has special meaning that current TTY (stdin/stdout) is
     used instead of TCP/IP.  A negative port number will disable the port.
     By analogy with pty(4) device, the dcons(4) acts as a slave device and
     ddccoonnsscchhaatt acts as a master device with tteellnneettdd.

     Typed characters are normally transmitted directly to dcons(4).  A escape
     character (the default is ‘~’ ) appearing as the first character of a
     line is an escape signal; the following are recognized:

     ~~..      Drop the connection and exit.

     ~~^^GG     Invoke kgdb on the terminal on which dconschat is running.

     ~~^^RR     Reset the target over FireWire if a reset address is registered
             in Configuration ROM.

     ~~^^ZZ     Suspend the dconschat process.

     The following options are supported.

     --bb      Translate Ctrl-C to ALT_BREAK (CR + ‘~’ + Ctrl-B) on gdb(1)
             (_p_o_r_t_s_/_d_e_v_e_l_/_g_d_b) port.

     --rr      Replay old buffer on connection.

     --vv      Verbose debug output.  Multiple --vv options increase verbosity.

     --ww      Listen on a wildcard address rather than localhost.

     --RR      Read-only.  Do not write anything to the dcons(4) buffer.

     --TT      Enable ad-hoc workaround for the TELNET protocol to remove unnec‐
             essary byte sequences.  It should be set when you access
             ddccoonnsscchhaatt using telnet(1).

     --11      One-shot.  Read available buffer, then exit.  This implies the --rr
             option.

     --ee _e_s_c_a_p_e_-_c_h_a_r
             Specify escape character.  The default is '~'.

     --hh _h_z   Specify polling rate.  The default value is 100.

     --CC _c_o_n_s_o_l_e___p_o_r_t
             Specify the console port.  The default value is 0 (stdin/stdout).

     --GG _g_d_b___p_o_r_t
             Specify gdb(1) (_p_o_r_t_s_/_d_e_v_e_l_/_g_d_b) port.  The default value is -1
             (disabled).

     --MM _c_o_r_e
             Specify core file.

     --NN _s_y_s_t_e_m
             Specify system file such as _/_b_o_o_t_/_k_e_r_n_e_l_/_k_e_r_n_e_l.

     --tt _t_a_r_g_e_t___e_u_i_6_4
             Specify the 64-bit extended unique identifier of the target, and
             use FireWire to access remote dcons(4).

     --aa _a_d_d_r_e_s_s
             Specify the physical I/O address of the dcons(4) buffer.  See
             dcons(4) for details.  If this option is not specified, ddccoonnsscchhaatt
             tries to get the address from the Configuration ROM on the tar‐
             get.  You are supposed to enable dcons_crom(4) on the target to
             omit this option.

     --uu _b_u_s___n_u_m
             Specify FireWire bus number.  The default is 0.

